; Direct tests of the helpers the stages share: the traversals of the TST and
; the CGT (traversals.ml), types and their substitution, signatures, overload
; ranking, lowering's type layouts, the runtime's ABI and what its structs
; measure (tests/runtime/abi), what stage 5's evaluator makes of the tree,
; how codegen reads a snapshot, the processor codegen tunes for and which targets it accepts, and
; how a build keeps its compiled runtime and links. The golden suites test the
; same code end to end; these say which helper broke, rather than where in a
; golden file the difference surfaced. They also check that semantics run twice in one process gives the
; same tree (it keeps no numbering from one check to the next), that the
; test rules' generator pairs every fixture with a golden file, and that the
; driver checks a stamp and keeps a file its rewrite did not create, and the
; C interface's front half (foreign_c.ml): `c.coda`'s patterns and paths,
; what a C compiler's include list says, and a C source compiled by the
; linked clang.
;
; Overloads, State, Type_layout, Emit, Build and stage 5's modules are not re-exported by their libraries'
; entry modules, so they are reached by the names dune gives them.

